# judge/judge.env.example: the agent judge's own settings file (template; example values only).
#
# Copy to ~/.config/judge/judge.env (or point $JUDGE_ENV at another file), mode 600. `judge/install.sh --apply`
# creates it, or MERGES into an existing one: it sets only the SITE_ENV= line and keeps every other line.
#
# Read by judge/lib/config.py on every hook call and runner run (precedence: environment > judge.env >
# site.env > built-in defaults), and loaded by the judge units as their environment (EnvironmentFile=), so hooks
# and units resolve the same values. Parsed, never sourced: KEY=value lines, `#` comments, optional quotes, no
# expansion.
#
# ALLOWED here: SITE_ENV= and the non-identifying policy knobs listed below, nothing else.
# NOT here: anything that identifies the site. JUDGE_SSH_ALIASES, JUDGE_INFRA_REPOS and JUDGE_REPO_DIR (absolute
# home paths), hosts, addresses, user names and secrets live in site.env, where scripts/check-sanitized.sh checks
# them. install.sh warns when it finds a site-identifying key in judge.env.

# Where the site values are. Without a resolvable site env (this line, $SITE_ENV, or ~/.config/deck/site.env) the
# frontier judge is REFUSED: nothing is sent and every request is judged locally (judge-findings warns).
SITE_ENV=~/.config/deck/site.env

# --- policy knobs (optional; each defaults as in judge/README.md "Configuration")
# JUDGE_MODE=frontier                    # frontier | local
# JUDGE_FRONTIER_DAILY_MAX=20            # frontier calls per UTC day
# JUDGE_FRONTIER_MAX_USD=2               # per-call --max-budget-usd
# JUDGE_FRONTIER_TIMEOUT=900             # seconds per frontier call
# JUDGE_FRONTIER_MODEL=                  # --model for the frontier CLI; empty = its default
# JUDGE_FRONTIER_EXTRA_ARGS="--setting-sources project"
# JUDGE_SENSITIVE_FRONTIER_CLAIMS=1      # sensitive completions also get a frontier claims-only review
# JUDGE_MIXED_MAX_SENSITIVE=3            # withheld sensitive paths an infra request may carry (0 = strict)
# JUDGE_LOCAL_MODEL=big                  # gateway alias of the local judge
# JUDGE_LOCAL_MAX_SEVERITY=medium        # cap for local-judge findings
# JUDGE_LOCAL_TIMEOUT=600
# JUDGE_LOCAL_MAX_TOKENS=4096
# JUDGE_CODE_REVIEW=1
# JUDGE_LOCAL_CODE_REVIEW=0
# JUDGE_PROBES=1
# JUDGE_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# JUDGE_INJECT_LOCAL=0
# JUDGE_INJECT_MIN_SEVERITY=medium
# JUDGE_STALL_MINUTES=15
# JUDGE_RUNAWAY_TOKENS=24000
# JUDGE_RUNAWAY_MINUTES=10
# JUDGE_ALERT_MIN_INTERVAL_S=900         # units only: seconds between two desktop alerts for one failed unit
